Subject: [PATCH 5/8] T71 F6 F7: the perspective, the cover, the cut list, the
 visualisation

setPerspective: a pinhole camera at eye height in the room; the engine's boxes (units
with fronts, plinths, end panels, worktops) painted farthest first and white-filled so a
nearer box covers what stands behind it; handles and unit numbers; NTS. Painter's
order, not a hidden-line pass, which is exact for boxes in a row along one wall.
setPaper: the cover (title, the job in one line, the sheet index, the revisions, the
conventions, the general notes, the picture fitted into its frame), the cut list
(every panel per unit from result.panels, fronts in magenta, paged down four columns
with cutListPages, the totals on the last sheet), the visualisation (the render in a
frame at its own aspect, the finishes beside it, or the sentence saying what it waits
for).

